1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,050
The Eiffel Tower.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:08,025
The Eiffel Tower was built for the 1889 World Fair and was initially intended to be temporary.

3
00:00:08,025 --> 00:00:14,337
Many Parisians condemned its design; a group of prominent artists publicly called it a monstrous eyesore.

4
00:00:14,337 --> 00:00:20,975
The tower was spared demolition because its 330-meter height proved ideal for radio telegraphy.

5
00:00:20,975 --> 00:00:25,550
Its antennas intercepted enemy communications during World War I.

6
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:32,000
Today, it is the most visited paid monument globally, welcoming nearly 7 million visitors annually.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,325
The tower was the world's tallest structure until 1930.

8
00:00:36,325 --> 00:00:44,300
The iron structure expands and contracts with temperature, increasing its height by approximately 15 centimeters in summer heat.

9
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:51,637
What began as a controversial exhibition structure has become the defining symbol of Paris and of French engineering worldwide.

